{
  "_about": [
    "Hand-labelled key for bench/onboard.py. Every label was derived from the source",
    "file's column semantics (the venue vocabularies in python/src/corpus/generate.py and",
    "the parser header conventions) and the canonical schema in",
    "python/src/inspector/mapping/canonical.py. Nothing here was produced by running the",
    "mapper. A null label means the correct outcome is to leave the column unassigned:",
    "value_date and client_id are populated by Harbormaster, never taken from a column;",
    "surplus price columns (prior settle, mark, theoretical) have no canonical slot; and a",
    "second instrument identifier (ISIN beside Symbol) has nowhere to go once the first is",
    "taken. Quarantine labels follow FR-30 and REQUIRED_BY_DOMAIN: a file is expected to be",
    "held when its client cannot be determined or a field the domain requires is absent.",
    "The seed and sha256 values pin the exact bytes that were labelled; the harness refuses",
    "to score a file whose bytes differ (xlsx carries a save timestamp, so it is unpinned).",
    "An 'either' group lists columns that are all legitimate carriers of one canonical field",
    "(Symbol and ISIN both identify the instrument): exactly one must take it, the rest stay",
    "unassigned, and the group is scored on that shape rather than on which carrier was chosen."
  ],
